...@../../../dev/d2/themes/sequence
# W09: late positive response can win only while original live premises remain valid.
shape: sequence_diagram
coord: Original fenced coordinator
issuer: Original issuer
ledger: Authoritative ledger
broker: Final broker
cancel: Authorized abort task
coord -> ledger: Exact ConsumePending already durable
coord -> issuer: Consume exact original grant
issuer -> issuer: Consume once
coord -> coord: Response timeout\nNo guessed success / holds retained
cancel -> cancel: Abort requested / scheduling delay
issuer -> coord: Late authenticated positive response
coord -> ledger: S4 original allowed-state CAS\nCurrent source / versions / lineage / fence
ledger -> coord: SendCommitted wins before abort
broker -> coord: Claim under current valid premise
coord -> ledger: S5 unique claim CAS
ledger -> coord: Claim durably spent
coord -> broker: Original one-use emission handle
cancel -> ledger: AbortNoDispatch CAS\nRequires absent claim
ledger -> cancel: Reject abort / claim already exists\nNo refund / no reopened row
broker -> broker: Final transport gate may still pass or fail
ledger.rule: "S4 winning alone does not defeat abort; S5 claim must win too.\nIf abort wins between S4 and S5, claim fails and no handle is issued.\nIf a required premise or original owner changed, the late callback cannot commit."

# Shared role accents; brand marks are confined to architecture headers.
coord.class: runtime
issuer.class: policy
ledger.class: ledger
broker.class: runtime
cancel.class: deny
ledger.rule.class: note
